{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-unibranch}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c3c32cb2b2a201e109e8e454cb06ed57ebf930cfc55ebb03dc4a8d2d765e59db", "source_text": "Local irreducibility", "source_text_hash": "sha256:509d5bd9114b6646078a1b3a85c10013b3c25538fddc17588b0ef0a06afec1a9", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ1:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-section-unibranch}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bef09784d81b6a5a009c7ab0267311ad7b142ce5c32a4da29e26626a497a44aa", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that in More on Algebra, Section <REF_0001>\nwe introduced the notion of a (geometrically) unibranch local ring.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a7c2a471e0bb63fde95f263b7073f4c2f5ba65225cad570d086fb19cd006c9f1", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ1:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[Chapter IV (6.15.1)]{EGA4}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "MATH_0011": "$X$", "MATH_0012": "$X$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-unibranch}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7d4b7c59bb4f07816370d26cf47f79e54bea6456de51e80facf8184d67e0598", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00fd79d959293e4c042d0ce4cbaab8a2ed64c95b0d126429709c67bfe68e7679", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002>. We say <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>unibranch at <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif the local ring <MATH_0005> is unibranch. We say <MATH_0006> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>geometrically unibranch at <MATH_0007><TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\nif the local ring <MATH_0008> is geometrically unibranch.\nWe say <MATH_0009> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>unibranch<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if <MATH_0010> is unibranch at all of its points.\nWe say <MATH_0011> is <TEXTITOPEN_0004>geometrically unibranch<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> if <MATH_0012> is\ngeometrically unibranch at all of its points.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fddf2d5f3ac2d042bc00ce098f2df11f31b142af9fe10be05df2c9c98862c563", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ2:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-unibranch}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-unibranch}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f6f82f04d36403eeb036d5c9236e217f4ca1a17dc2ef9b5f6aa9261e51810370", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4db466670c7b972f86178fc376fcdd87ad659a48623fb85d17a7e7955c84ce66", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nTo be sure, it can happen that a local ring <MATH_0001> is geometrically unibranch\n(in the sense of\nMore on Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>)\nbut the scheme <MATH_0002> is not geometrically unibranch in the sense\nof Definition <REF_0002>. For example this happens\nif <MATH_0003> is the local ring at the vertex of the cone over an irreducible\nplane curve which has ordinary double point singularity (a node).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49209495c97ef037f292cf68d2b77a73df4bb9895fbba916ee42b8b35175c8ad", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ1:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-normal-geometrically-unibranch}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:904374e831c575cfaf7c7bbda081ad7e3c41740c8d81daacee95b5d0b3e18ec2", "source_text": "A normal scheme is geometrically unibranch.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:26d5f4c44df49e7d22f63194053653f689a3f26d973a8a623f0188c719c9da15", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ3:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0BQ1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-unibranch}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b1befb26cddb03334f30e4bd604fa9132cb986090ead363f907931c491428d4a", "source_text": "This follows from the definitions. Namely, a scheme\nis normal if the local rings are normal domains. It is immediate\nfrom the More on Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>\nthat a local normal domain is geometrically unibranch.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c5a0a876658ef3267839c36b708698940f1c91512fdfa4cc5947ca6893717131", "unit_id": "tag:0BQ3:proof"}
